  "notes": "{押|お}す is a godan verb meaning to push, press, or stamp.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {押|お}される (passive, to be pushed)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ボタンを{押|お}す: to press a button\n- {扉|とびら}を{押|お}す: to push a door\n- ハンコを{押|お}す: to stamp a seal\n- {印鑑|いんかん}を{押|お}す: to affix one's seal\n\nANTONYM:\n{引|ひ}く (to pull)\n\nDOOR SIGNS:\n- {押|お}す: Push\n- {引|ひ}く: Pull\n\nNOTE:\nStamping a seal ({判子|はんこ}/{印鑑|いんかん}) is common in Japan for official documents instead of signatures.",
